.page source 1 run the commands of a file in this shell
.alias .

# SYNOPSIS
*source* _FILE_ [_ARGUMENT_...]
*.* _FILE_ [_ARGUMENT_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`source` (also spelled `.`) is a gapsh builtin. It reads _FILE_ and runs its commands in the current shell, so assignments, functions and aliases it defines stay. A _FILE_ without a slash is looked for in the directories of `PATH`. The arguments become the positional parameters while the file runs.

# EXIT STATUS
The status of the last command, 127 if the file cannot be read, 2 if no file is named.

# EXAMPLES
    . ~/.gaprc
    source /Hakurei/etc/profile

# SEE ALSO
eval(1), gapsh(1)
